  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: rrdtool\n  version: \"1.10.3\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/oetiker/rrdtool-1.x/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 3f98a07cf00a16a811716f925e0ccb105a51183743bbd65b997aea11c9e15943\n  patches:\n    # Link libcairo directly; rrdtool uses it but only links -lpangocairo\n    - link-libcairo.patch\n\nbuild:\n  # Fails with \"Bad CPU type in executable\" when cross-compiling\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - win\n    - ppc64le\n  python:\n    skip_pyc_compilation:\n      - if: osx and arm64\n        then: share/rrdtool/examples/stripes.py\n  dynamic_linking:\n    # Everything librrd links is a declared dependency and every declared\n    # dependency is linked, so hold that line and fail the build if it slips.\n    overlinking_behavior: error\n    overdepending_behavior: error\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: unix\n      then: gnuconfig\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - autoconf\n    - automake\n    - harfbuzz\n    - make\n    - libtool\n    # msgfmt/autopoint to compile & bootstrap the .po catalogs; runs on the\n    # build machine, so build- (not host-) side for correct cross-compilation\n    - gettext-tools\n    - pkg-config\n    # Required for \"make check\"\n    - coreutils\n    - bc\n  host:\n    - cairo\n    - glib\n    - libpng\n    - libxml2-devel\n    - pango\n    # gettext is external (AM_GNU_GETTEXT); libintl is part of glibc on Linux\n    # but a separate library on macOS, so it is only needed there.\n    - if: osx\n      then: libintl-devel\n  run:\n    # pango's run-export already applies a compatible pin; libintl has no\n    # run-export, so the macOS runtime dependency must be listed explicitly.\n    - if: osx\n      then: libintl\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      # End-to-end: create -> update -> graph. `graph` renders through\n      # cairo/pango, so it also proves libcairo is linked and usable at runtime.\n      - rrdtool create test.rrd --step 300 DS:x:GAUGE:600:U:U RRA:AVERAGE:0.5:1:24\n      - rrdtool update test.rrd N:42\n      - rrdtool graph test.png --start end-2h DEF:x=test.rrd:x:AVERAGE LINE1:x#ff0000\n      - test -s test.png\n  - package_contents:\n      # strict: every packaged file must match a pattern below, so anything\n      # unexpected (e.g. the stray fontconfig cache we now clean up) fails.\n      strict: true\n      bin:\n        - rrdtool\n        - rrdcached\n        - rrdcgi\n        - rrdcreate\n        - rrdinfo\n        - rrdupdate\n      lib:\n        - librrd\n      include:\n        - rrd.h\n        - rrd_client.h\n        - rrd_format.h\n      files:\n        # Broad, directory-level globs so new examples/locales or a soname bump\n        # are absorbed while strict still flags anything outside these paths.\n        - bin/rrd*\n        - include/rrd*.h\n        - lib/librrd.*\n        - lib/pkgconfig/librrd.pc\n        - lib/systemd/system/rrdcached.*\n        - share/locale/*/LC_MESSAGES/*.mo\n        - share/rrdtool/**\n\nabout:\n  license: GPL-2.0-or-later\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Round Robin Database Tool\n  description: |\n    RRDtool is a little program for easily maintaining a database of\n    time-series data. It comes with a charting program for drawing\n    pretty graphs based on the data stored.\n  homepage: https://www.rrdtool.org\n  repository: https://github.com/oetiker/rrdtool-1.x/\n  documentation: https://www.rrdtool.org/doc/index.en.html\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - chrisburr\n",
